<title>FRANCE: Matra Marconi Space wins $100 mln contract.</title>
<headline>Matra Marconi Space wins $100 mln contract.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>European satellite maker Matra Marconi Space (MMS) said on Thursday it has won a $100 million contract from satellite operator Intelsat.</p>
<p>MMS is a joint venture between Lagardere Groupe and General Electric Co Plc (GEC).</p>
<p>The contract is for a direct broadcast television satellite, Intelsat K-TV, which would be the first non-U.S. made satellite ordered by Intelsat, which is based in the United States, MMS said in a statement. The satellite will serve the Asia/Pacific zone and will be delivered at the end of 1998.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
